          "available": "For every elliptic curve over C, integration of an invariant differential identifies its complex Lie group with C/Lambda for its full rank-two period lattice. The torsion subgroup is (1/m)Lambda/Lambda.",
          "needed": "For the actual real curve and a real invariant differential, obtain the full period lattice and finite torsion identifications before proving integral conjugation splitting.",
